// What an attack-simulation campaign leaves behind in email telemetry.
//
// SURFACE: Defender Advanced Hunting (security.microsoft.com). Column is
// Timestamp, NOT TimeGenerated. These tables are XDR-native and FREE - confirmed
// by the store-partition census on 2026-07-26 (kql/sentinel/store-partition-diff.kql),
// where EmailEvents and EmailUrlInfo appear in the Defender run and drop out of
// the Azure/Log Analytics run.
//
// THE FINDING (Lab 09, POS-037), measured 2026-07-26:
//   The simulation PAYLOAD appears in NEITHER table. The training assignment
//   notifications that bracket it appear in BOTH, normally, which is what proves
//   the tables were working rather than empty.
//
//   EmailEvents  -> 2 rows, both "Training assignment notification" from
//                   attacksimulationtraining.com, ThreatTypes empty, Delivered.
//   EmailUrlInfo -> 4 rows, all security.microsoft.com training links.
//   Absent       -> the Credential Harvest payload (sender templatern.com) and
//                   its landing URL (sharepointle.com), delivered 3 hours earlier
//                   and inside the query window.
//
//   Not ingestion lag: records from 8 minutes prior were present while one from
//   3 hours prior was not. Under lag the NEWER rows would be missing.
//
// CONSEQUENCE: a simulation cannot be hunted. No row means no hunting query, no
// custom detection rule, no analytics rule, no ATT&CK mapping. Attack simulation
// training tests USERS - it is not evidence about detection coverage, and running
// one proves nothing about whether real phishing would be caught.
EmailEvents
| where Timestamp > ago(6h)
| project Timestamp, SenderFromDomain, RecipientEmailAddress, Subject,
          DeliveryAction, DeliveryLocation, ThreatTypes
| order by Timestamp desc

// The URL half of the same question. Run both - one table alone cannot
// distinguish "payload absent" from "this table is empty anyway."
// EmailUrlInfo
// | where Timestamp > ago(6h)
// | project Timestamp, Url, UrlDomain
// | order by Timestamp desc

// Control check. If the notifications are ALSO missing, the tables are not
// reporting and nothing above can be concluded.
// EmailEvents
// | where Timestamp > ago(24h)
// | summarize Events = count(), Latest = max(Timestamp) by SenderFromDomain
